[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Hold {select} to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
{start} (Escape) pauses and backs out of the game's menus. Tap {start} twice to quick save and hold it to quick load.
{south} jumps, {east} crouches, {west} reloads and, held, uses: open doors, pick things up, read notes. {right} taps the use key. {rs} is melee, {l3} sprints, {up} is the flashlight and {select} the inventory. {lb} and {rb} step through your weapons; {north} steps forward too.
Hold {lt} for the weapon's alt fire (aim). The right stick turns more finely while it's held.
Cry of Fear has its own joystick support, but it only turns left and right and would fight this setup. Turn the joystick off in the game's controls options, so only the keys and mouse count.
These are the Half-Life style default keys, written from memory and not checked in the game (melee, the flashlight, lean, quick save and quick load especially). Check them in the game's Controls menu, which lets you rebind every one.
{guide} still works over the game: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard and {guide} + {lb} the media controls.
If the game stops answering the pad, check that Steam Input or another remapper isn't also running for it.'''

